WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.139
Is Disney sticking by the all new, very blue
Genie?

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:06.620
Or is the House of Mouse already denouncing
its own creation?

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.630
The company kept quiet after the internet
completely torched Will Smith following the

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.130
newest live-action Aladdin trailer drop, but
now, Disney has come forward to address the

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.529
blue Genie debacle.

00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:20.660
It wasn't long ago that Disney summoned up
the second trailer for its upcoming live-action

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.820
remake of Aladdin, an updated version of the
1992 animated classic from director Guy Ritchie.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.869
But the very vocal response to the trailer
from online viewers may have caught studio

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:34.500
executives off guard — especially the reaction
to the Genie reveal money shot.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.000
Some people must have liked it, but the consensus
seemed clear:

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:38.920
"Terrible…"

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.100
In addition to the new face of the Genie,
the sneak peeks of movie have brought audiences

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.830
their first glimpses of fresh-faced actor
Mena Massoud as Aladdin, the scrappy street

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:52.830
rat who sweeps a royal princess off her feet
with the help of a few white lies and a magic

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:53.920
flying carpet.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.210
That princess, Jasmine, is being played by
Naomi Scott, who you may recognize from the

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.780
cast of the 2017 Power Rangers movie.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.601
The previews for the movie have also offered
looks at the fictional city of Agrabah, as

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:09.850
well as a glimpse of Marwan Kenzari as the
movie's nefarious Grand Vizier, Jafar.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.340
Perhaps most recognizable is the glittering
Cave of Wonders, and the ever-important golden

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.890
lamp that sits within it.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.140
But, much to many peoples' dismay, the most
terrifying image from the second sneak peek

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.390
is a brief, kind of I can never unsee that
moment of actor Will Smith as the Genie a

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:30.649
blue-skinned magical being who looks... um…
bluer in real-life than anyone could have

00:01:30.649 --> 00:01:31.649
thought possible.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:32.960
Viewer responses were not great.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.900
"I HATE IT!"

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.260
After the internet dragged Smith and the remake's
new Genie look, Disney kept quiet.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.360
What might happen, now that the company knew
people were rejecting this important investment?

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.969
Would they address the hate, or keep their
lips sealed until the movie came out?

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:50.009
Could they tweak their approach to the Genie,
maybe by making him look a little bit more

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.560
real?

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.560
That remains to be seen.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:56.240
But for now, the company has come forward
to at least address the big blue Genie debacle.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.189
In a statement released to USA Today, a little
over a week after the second teaser saw release,

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:05.509
Disney defended Smith's Genie in broad terms
without getting into the specifics of viewers'

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:07.119
shocked reactions.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.640
Reactions that ranged from "that looks scary,"
or "that looks fake," to...

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.040
"Wow, that's… so gross."

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.420
The company attempted to beat the bad buzz
by affirming its confidence in both the new

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.870
interpretation of the Genie character, and
the live-action Aladdin project as a whole.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:22.870
The statement read,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.879
"We have one of the most anticipated films
of the year and are confident that audiences

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:30.900
will fall in love with the Genie and all of
the characters when it hits the big screen

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.420
this May."

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.250
It's not exactly a shocker that Disney is
sticking to its guns with Smith's Genie.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.569
It'd be more surprising if they actually agreed
with the criticism.

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:40.870
What else are they supposed to do, cancel
the movie?

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.420
"What?

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:41.960
No.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.220
I mean, maybe."

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.920
Despite the lousy first reactions to one of
the film's main characters, there's plenty

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.400
of Aladdin that we've simply yet to see meaning
there's also hope that the Genie could work

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.620
just fine in context so long as people are
still willing to give the movie a shot.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.620
But considering all the skepticism in the
air around these teasers, that's no guarantee.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.890
Whether audiences are hype for it or not,
the film's creative team is likely putting

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:08.989
all available resources into ensuring the
live-action Aladdin is as shining, shimmering,

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:10.930
and splendid as it possibly can be.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.260
It's just a project with a lot to live up
to especially for Smith, taking over a role

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.300
first embodied by the late, larger-than-life
Robin Williams.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.140
It's possible that audiences were going to
judge Smith harshly no matter what approach

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.340
the filmmakers took, holding his performance
to a high standard whether the effects looked

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.240
flawless or not.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.920
The former Fresh Prince has enormous shoes
to fill, but you can't say that he's not trying.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.920
As he said in an interview with Entertainment
Weekly,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.099
"...I got to sing, I got to rap, I got to
dance, I got to do action sequences — it

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:42.269
was everything that I've trained and learned
how to do over the last 30 years of entertainment

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:44.650
and I got to it use all in playing the Genie."

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.960
Maybe the Genie's weird looks will keep people
from getting on board with the remake.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.980
Or maybe the world will be as charmed as Princess
Jasmine on a magic carpet ride.

00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:56.700
To find out what happens, we'll simply have
to wait until Aladdin arrives in theaters

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.720
on May 24.

